{"cause":"The replay memo key contains only PR and head. replay_state returns skipped for the old checker-change attempt, and replay returns before reevaluating the current base/head checker comparison. It never invalidates that decision on a base/replayer change. retry_lines also excludes a current head whose memo is skipped.","duty":"47cdf978c4d322b1f7c386ee19ee897741ea32712104d91d2f52a50539d1aa2c","item":0,"limits":["This is a bounded obligation review and fixture reproduction, not an exhaustive repository audit.","No production replay checker seed was read, and no live installed-waker replay, live Codex wake, or sandbox isolation was exercised. Fixture keys and mock reviewer calls are not production attestations.","The existing passing suites and killed mutants do not cover resumption of a skipped replay after checker adoption at an unchanged PR head.","The challenge is of obligation closure item 0; it is not a warrant-review/finding@1 record or a claim that unrelated obligations fail."],"master":"7b46fef35e03b34fc0dcd90fbcdc731eab6144b8","obligation_gap":"D requires the review replay checker to replay the reviewer's test at each head. This head remains without observations even after its checker bytes match the adopted base and the generated fixture seed is usable. An unrelated head change or manual memo removal must not be needed to resume a skip whose reason has gone away.","references":["s0fractal/warrant#204","c190377a504d841df9f7bfd565d6abec68055145"],"reproduction":{"causal_control_change":"In a separate source copy, after state, why = self.replay_state(doc), if state == \"skipped\" and doc.get(\"base\") != base, set doc = None and reevaluate replay_state(doc). No repository source was changed.","expected":"After adoption, the next eligible replay runs the checker and files FAIL at the original finding head and PASS at its answering head, without manual memo deletion.","method":"Git fixture using the repository's review_replay_test.pr_world and Waker.tick, with due discovery and Codex execution mocked. First skip a fixed PR head whose checker differs from the base; adopt the exact PR checker bytes in a sibling base commit; tick four times beyond backoff without moving the PR head. Compare real Git blobs and the finding observations. Then remove only the fixture skip memo and tick once.","observed":"At both subject and M, checker blobs match but four later ticks make zero checker calls, keep state skipped, and leave observations empty. Removing only the fixture memo immediately runs one checker and pushes two observations.","python":"import json\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(sys.argv[1]).resolve()\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / 'tests'))\nimport review_replay_test as Q\n\n# The PR already contains the current checker. The old base does not; a sibling\n# base commit later adopts precisely those checker bytes, with the PR head held fixed.\nf = Q.pr_world(head_files={Q.WAKER.CHECKER_FILE: (ROOT / Q.WAKER.CHECKER_FILE).read_text()})\ntry:\n    Q.flaky(f, 0)\n    base = [f.start]\n    f.w.fetch = lambda: base[0]\n    f.w.due = lambda b: {'due': [dict(Q.due(f), base=b)], 'not_due': []}\n    first = Q.WAKER.tick(f.w, False)\n    before = {'checker_runs': len(f.runs), 'wakes': len(f.codex.calls), 'lines': first}\n    f.git('checkout', '-q', '--detach', f.start)\n    adopted = f.commit('adopt checker on base without merging this PR', {\n        Q.WAKER.CHECKER_FILE: (ROOT / Q.WAKER.CHECKER_FILE).read_text()})\n    Q.git('-C', str(f.dir), 'push', '-q', str(f.origin), adopted + ':refs/heads/master')\n    Q.git('-C', str(f.w.mirror), 'fetch', '-q', str(f.origin), '+refs/heads/master:refs/heads/master')\n    base[0] = adopted\n    matching = f.w.blob(adopted, Q.WAKER.CHECKER_FILE) == f.w.blob(f.head, Q.WAKER.CHECKER_FILE)\n    later = []\n    for _ in range(4):\n        f.now[0] += Q.WAKER.BACKOFF * 8 + 1\n        later.append(Q.WAKER.tick(f.w, False))\n    memo_path, memo = f.w.replay_memo(Q.due(f))\n    after = {'checker_blobs_match': matching, 'checker_runs': len(f.runs),\n             'wakes': len(f.codex.calls), 'observations': Q.at_commit(f, Q.tip(f)).findings[f.cid].observed,\n             'memo_state': f.w.replay_state(memo)[0], 'lines': later}\n    # Control: the guard permits the run at this base; remove just the fixture's\n    # old memo, leaving its code, configuration, seed, branch and head unchanged.\n    memo_path.unlink()\n    control = Q.WAKER.tick(f.w, False)\n    observations = Q.at_commit(f, Q.tip(f)).findings[f.cid].observed\n    result = {'at': sys.argv[2], 'before': before, 'after_adoption': after,\n              'control': {'checker_runs': len(f.runs), 'observed_commits': sorted(observations), 'lines': control},\n              'defect_reproduced': matching and after['checker_runs'] == 0 and not after['observations']\n                                    and len(observations) == 2}\n    print(json.dumps(result, indent=2))\n    assert after['checker_runs'] == 1 and after['observations'], 'adoption must resume the skipped replay without deleting its memo'\nfinally:\n    f.close()\n","regression":"The included Python probe asserts the expected behavior and exits 1 on the subject and M. A separate external control copy that reevaluates a skipped memo when its base changes exits 0; it is a causal control, not a proposed or reviewed production fix.","results":{"control":{"after_adoption":{"checker_blobs_match":true,"checker_runs":1,"lines":[["2027-01-15T10:00:01+00:00 base master 7aff40f828cf: 1 due, 0 not due","  DUE #1 c136a8d99895: replay: 2 observation(s) by checker sha256:c0a8c6593841 pushed as d72e378c327a on pr1","  0 obligation closure(s) due for codex's verdict"],["2027-01-15T12:00:02+00:00 base master 7aff40f828cf: 1 due, 0 not due","  DUE #1 c136a8d99895: replay: 2 observation(s) by checker sha256:c0a8c6593841 pushed as d72e378c327a on pr1; done: woken 2027-01-15T08:00:00+00:00, codex exited 0","  0 obligation closure(s) due for codex's verd